{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a depth-first search reports, in order, with the classification of CLRS §22.3."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DepthFirstSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vertex is discovered, then every edge out of it is reported once per copy, then it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finished. An edge to an undiscovered vertex is a tree edge, and the search continues from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex before the next edge. An edge to a vertex discovered but not yet finished is a back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge; a self-loop is one. An edge to a finished vertex is a forward edge when that vertex was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discovered later than the edge’s source (a descendant; a repeated tree edge is one), and a cross"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge otherwise."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/depthfirstsearchevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DepthFirstSearchEven